nDate":"2025-02-11","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Natural Resources."},"laws":[],"number":"1192","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Public Lands and Natural Resources","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"F000472","district":18,"fullName":"Rep. Franklin, Scott [R-FL-18]","party":"R","state":"FL"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-11","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This bill prohibits the Big Cypress National Preserve in Florida from being designated as wilderness or as a component of the National Wilderness Preservation System. The National Park Service currently manages Big Cypress National&nbsp;Preserve, which is a freshwater swamp ecosystem of 729,000 acres.&nbsp;</p><p>In general, development activities, commercial activities, permanent structures, and roads are prohibited in wilderness areas. In contrast, natural preserves typically allow some&nbsp;development activities, such as hunting or oil and gas exploration.</p>","updateDate":"2026-02-26T16:58:21Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"To ensure that Big Cypress National Preserve may not be designated as wilderness or as a component of the National Wilderness Preservation System, and for other purposes.","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-18T00:01:58Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-18T00:01:58Z"}
